; an `alias` of the loading file gave a theory's symbol another meaning: `alias Nat ∅`, then `load
; natural` made every fact about `Nat` one about `∅` (`∀ n ∈ Nat (n + 1 = n)` was proved, also with
; --strict); `alias false true` before `load prop` made `false` true (found by the soundness hunt,
; 2026-10-14; `validate_against_loader`)
expect "EvalError" "is an alias of `true` here"
    alias false true
    load prop
load set
alias Leer ∅                  ; an alias of a name of its own: fine
expect "EvalError" "is an alias of `∅` here"
    alias Nat ∅
    load natural
